{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Held-out TDD contract cards (orchestrator-owned):\n\n1) retry convergence — authoritative contract: shipped five-attempt workflow loop + ticket AC1; precondition: local HEAD ahead while a deterministic real competitor advances origin before each of the first five push attempts; production path: push_tickets_branch against real temporary refs; tier: integration/real git because reachability and data-loss are the mechanism; postcondition: exactly six pushes, remote HEAD equals local HEAD, both local and all competitor commits remain ancestors; negative control: success before exhaustion performs no terminal push; gate: make test.\n\n2) strict failure matrix — authoritative contract: AC2/4/5; precondition: semantic fault seam selects each real early-return/terminal branch; production path: push_tickets_branch(strict=True); tier: in-process unit with real state where count/reachability matters; postcondition: catchable PushDeliveryError with pinned reason/detail/unpushed count, no sys.exit/stream write; collateral: HEAD/worktree/event set unchanged; paired best-effort call returns None; gate: make test.\n\n3) process boundary — authoritative contract: AC3/7; precondition: real local policy-rejecting origin and one unpushed commit; production path: python -m rebar._store.push push --tracker ... --strict; tier: subprocess; postcondition: nonzero stderr includes reason/detail/count, commit remains reachable, no event/BRIDGE_ALERT file; gate: make test.\n\n4) caller continuity — authoritative contract: AC6; precondition: each semantic caller reaches its shipped push seam; tier: in-process contract tests because call argument/default is the contract; postcondition: event append, batch append, import, close, two delete paths, two compact paths, and claim omit strict or reach strict=False and retain legacy result/disposition.\n\nSurface parity: private module CLI=in scope via subprocess; MCP/API tools=out of strict scope because no new strict surface and existing operations stay best-effort (covered through shared core callers); library facade=existing public operations in scope for continuity, direct strict remains private; automated callers=in scope via full inventory; dual-direction=inbound pull/reconcile out of scope because this leaf changes outbound delivery only. No bespoke concurrency harness: convergence extends the existing shared two-clone regression suite."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786148803956592001,"uuid":"4281eada-0f24-43a2-bc3a-a58df4d2b41a"}